<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI24-BLOCK-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI24-BLOCK-004" ;
  triage:title "RULE-002 function-length violation in crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/post_write_router.rs dispatch()" ;
  triage:description "dispatch() in crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/post_write_router.rs spans lines 14-103 (90 lines), exceeding the project's 80-line RULE-002 function-length threshold. This function was newly introduced by this sprint's PostWriteRouter extraction (commit 1daef214031fffa82d422862025086ae697b3251, closing AI24-IMPORTANT-001/002). Confirmed by CI: gh pr checks 630 shows Just lint failing on macos, ubuntu, and windows at this exact head. post_write_router.rs is a brand-new file containing only two functions (dispatch at lines 14-103, record_unconfirmed_delivery at lines 107-125); only dispatch() exceeds the threshold, so the pattern does not recur elsewhere in the new file or module. Correlation across ordered worktrees found this file present, byte-identical, and still violating on feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution (head b435fa6e), which has merged s24 forward unchanged. The file does not yet exist on feature/pAI-s26-peer-write-deadline, s27, s28, s29, or s30 (git show HEAD:<path> fails there), confirming those branches have not merged s24's PostWriteRouter refactor forward yet and therefore have no occurrence to record. NOTE FOR TEAM-LEAD: a near-duplicate record AI24-BLOCK-101.ttl already exists in this findings directory for the same violation (same file, same function, same commit), but with only a single s24 occurrence, orderIndex 24, and dispatch_ready=false; this record supersedes it with full s24/s25 correlation and dispatch_ready=true. Recommend reconciling/closing AI24-BLOCK-101 as a duplicate of AI24-BLOCK-004 once aggregated." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "architecture/function-size" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T02:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-26T02:19:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T14:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
